spec:
  grid: 24x24 square (all examples identical)
  pattern:
    symmetry: full D4 (horizontal, vertical, both diagonals) — 78 distinct orbits (12 size-4 on axes/diagonals, 66 size-8)
    colors: 7-9 distinct non-zero colors (1-9); color 0 never used in the pattern
    structure: each D4 orbit assigned one random color; moderate spatial autocorrelation (~2x random baseline) [observed]
  missing_region:
    shape: solid rectangle of color-0 pixels
    dimensions: 3-8 rows x 3-8 cols, area 9-42
    position: anywhere in the grid; may touch edges; no axis-crossing constraint [observed]
    solvability: every missing pixel must have >=1 non-missing orbit mate (observed min = 3)
  output: the missing rectangle only (not the full repaired grid), no color 0

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first — build full D4-symmetric 24x24 pattern, then carve a missing rectangle
  steps:
    1. Choose k=7-9 non-zero colors from 1-9.
    2. Build fundamental domain (triangle r in [0,11], c in [r,11], 78 cells). Assign each cell a random color from k.
    3. Expand to full 24x24 grid via D4 orbit mapping.
    4. Pick random rectangle dims h=3-8, w=3-8. Pick random top-left (r0,c0) with r0+h<=24, c0+w<=24.
    5. Verify solvability — every cell in the rectangle has >=1 non-zero orbit mate outside it. Retry placement if not.
    6. Zero out the rectangle to produce input. Extract the original rectangle values as output.
```
